    "body": "Excuse the very late reply! I totally missed the conversation about this.\r\n\r\n@domfarolino wrote:\r\n> Regarding a \"configurable\" alternative, which were you thinking:\r\n> \r\n> * Adding something to the API (if so, I think I'm against that), or...\r\n> * Allowing implementations to basically choose what to do with scripting enabled/disabled, and not specify its relationship to lazy loading\r\n\r\nThe latter. The note about the relationship between scripting enabled/disabled and lazy loading should be replaced by a general hint that user agents should implement some way to let the user control whether lazy loading is enabled/disabled for the reasons mentioned earlier. _How_ they do it can be let up to them but the spec. might still provide hints for possible options, i.e. binding it to scripting vs. an individual option or the integration into a general tracking protection concept.\r\n\r\nSebastian",
